  "worked_solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $1$ and $6$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+6=7.$",
